## What run 2 adds

1. 🔴 **A configuration change applied dynamically, while the device is operating, is saved and
   restored exactly like any other.** vlan48's address moved `.66` -> `.70` with no restart, was
   written, survived a 60 s cold boot, and came back with its full L3 identity -- including the
   source address of its own ICMP unreachables -- before anything was typed into the device.
   **T47192's reboot-persistence item is no longer NOT MEASURED.** "Dynamic" on this platform
   does not mean "temporary".
2. 🔬 **An SVI's own ICMP host-unreachable source address is a free, exact discriminator for
   which address an interface currently holds.** One leg to two addresses gives a matched pair
   -- echo reply from the address that exists, type 3 code 1 from the one that does not, sourced
   from the live one -- so the subject and its control are read from the same four rows. It
   needed no extra tooling and it is reusable for any address-change case.
3. 🔬 **A rebooted SVI sends a duplicate-address probe for its own address**
   (`who-has 10.38.22.70 tell 10.38.22.70`), which distinguishes an interface brought up from
   saved configuration from one that was merely never torn down.
4. 🔬 **Third hit of the post-reload settle trap in one hour** (T33380 run 2, T33386 run 2, this
   run): the first post-boot ping was 1 of 4, the second 4 of 4. Ping to 4/4 on every leg before
   reading any leg after a reload.
5. **Two of run 1's three NOT MEASURED items remain NOT MEASURED, deliberately** -- file-driven
   configuration needs a root write to the box's `/tftproot` (STANDING-ORDERS §4), and the
   mid-flow timing number needs a tool that does not exist in `tools/`. Neither was improvised.

